# The changelog is an append-only list, and every branch appends to the
# same few groups: two branches each adding a bullet conflict on the
# insertion point, which is a conflict with nothing to decide. `union`
# resolves it by keeping both sides' added lines, in the order
# base-then-ours, and it is built into git — nobody has to configure
# anything for it to apply.
#
# It applies to rebases too, which is where it earns its keep here, and
# it has a price worth knowing: this file now never conflicts at all, so
# the same existing entry edited on two branches merges in silence rather
# than being flagged. That is why nothing here states how many entries it
# has — a count is exactly such an edit, and union would have kept both
# numbers. CONTRIBUTING.md carries the rest of the reasoning.
#
# `RELEASE_NOTES.md` is the other subject of this rule in every sibling
# and is absent here, this repository releasing nothing. A rule whose
# subject the tree does not hold is not copied in ahead of it.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
